  "summary": "DOAC dose review (week of 10/19/2026) is finished under RBC-PHARM-07: all 7 patients reviewed. Each change has a progress note citing its sources.\n\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5 → 5 mg BID. She meets no dose criteria, and the itraconazole course ended 08/14 (St. Brigid ID letter).\n- pt-0003 Delgado: I first reduced rivaroxaban to 15 mg on an outside creatinine of 160 µmol/L. St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (analyzer fault), giving CrCl 59.9. I reversed the change; he is back on 20 mg daily (mr-t0013) and a correction note is filed.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5 → 2.5 mg BID because of active itraconazole. He meets no dose criteria.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: apixaban 5 → 2.5 mg BID. A St. Brigid creatinine that arrived during the review (150 µmol/L = 1.70 mg/dL), plus age 82, makes 2 criteria.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15 → 20 mg daily. CrCl is 56.1 on actual body weight; the May reduction had used ideal body weight. A portal message gives a home-scale weight of 185 lb. That isn't a measured weight under the policy, so the dose stays. At that weight CrCl would be about 49, so I recommended a clinic weight and creatinine at the next visit.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: rivaroxaban 20 → 15 mg daily. A new creatinine of 1.25 (drawn 10/22) gives CrCl 43.6.\n- pt-0002 Vance: on the review data apixaban went 2.5 → 5 mg BID (1 criterion, age 82). A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived reporting itraconazole started 10/22, so I changed it to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0014) and filed a correction note.\n\nNo other medications were changed, including the itraconazole orders.\n\nI closed the 5 inbox items that came in during the review. Nothing else arrived after that.\n\nTwo practical points:\n- The new rivaroxaban orders keep \"once daily\", but the change tool has no field for timing instructions, so \"with the evening meal\" may not appear on them. It is in each progress note; please check the order sigs.\n- For pt-0041 and pt-0002, the apixaban dose should be rechecked when the itraconazole courses end.",
